        reportYear: 2025,
        severity: 'critical',
        parameter: `Cost, schedule and water yield of the ₹23,251-crore Yettinahole drinking water scheme`,
        finding: `The Yettinahole project — designed to supply drinking water to the dry districts of Kolar, Chikkaballapura, Tumkur and Ramanagara — has seen its cost balloon 2.8× from ₹8,323.50 crore to ₹23,251.66 crore after two DPR revisions, and remains incomplete after 10 years with no water delivered to the target districts. The Government provided only 25–54% of annual budget requirements during 2018-23. A design change from 10 TMC to 2 TMC storage added ₹621.45 crore in avoidable extra cost. The projected water yield of 32.15 TMC was found to be overestimated against a realistic 24.70 TMC.`,
        actual: `Cost ballooned 2.8× (₹8,323 Cr → ₹23,251 Cr) after two DPR revisions; 10 years incomplete; only 25–54% annual budget provided; ₹621.45 Cr avoidable cost from design change; water yield overestimated (32.15 TMC vs actual 24.70 TMC).`,
        reportExcerpt: `"[Cost revised] from ₹8,323.50 crore to ₹12,912.36 crore in February 2014 and again to ₹23,251.66 crore in January 2023. Project works are still under progress and far from completion and intended benefit delivery… The Project suffered from financial constraints as the Government provided only 25 to 54 per cent of the budget requirements… VJNL faces financial uncertainty regarding the ₹7,954.63 crore required for completing the Project."`,
        sourceUrl: 'https://cag.gov.in/uploads/download_audit_report/2025/1.-FINAL-PRINTABLE-BOND-COPY-24.12.2025-(ENGLISH)-0697c9e632f2512.57145486.pdf',
