        finding: `Smart City projects in Karnataka's five selected cities saw funds diverted from their designated purpose: ₹1,462.67 crore was spent under the Pan City component against a ₹817.42 crore allocation — a 79% excess driven by diversion from other components. 30% of originally planned Area-Based Development projects were cancelled or modified. Centralised Command and Control Centres were operationalised at only ₹19.08 crore against ₹60.22 crore required. ₹2.69 crore in interest earned on Central grant funds was not remitted to Consolidated Funds; ₹2.56 crore was overpaid in contracts.`,
