        parameter: `FHTC delivery, water quality monitoring and long-term sustainability`,
        finding: `Karnataka provided FHTCs to only 47.62 lakh (66%) of 72.14 lakh targeted households as of November 2024, leaving 24.52 lakh families without piped water. The State received just 45% (₹11,189 crore) of its ₹24,819.48 crore central allocation because it couldn't utilise what had already been released. Not one of the 31 district-level and 48 taluk-level laboratories was equipped to test all 13 prescribed water quality parameters. Five villages were prematurely declared 100% FHTC-complete on the dashboard while works were still ongoing.`,
        actual: `47.62 lakh FHTCs vs 72.14 lakh target (66%); only ₹11,189 Cr of ₹24,819 Cr central allocation received; 0 of 31 district labs equipped for all 13 quality parameters; 5 villages falsely certified 100% complete; community contribution: ₹22.57 Cr of ₹1,594.90 Cr expected (1.4%).`,
        reportExcerpt: `"FHTCs were provided to 47.62 lakh (66 per cent) HHs as of November 2024… none of the 31 district level and 48 taluk level laboratories in the State [were equipped to test all 13 prescribed parameters]… community contribution collected was ₹22.57 crore against the estimated ₹1,594.90 crore… [five villages] declared 100 per cent completion [while works were still incomplete]."`,
