        finding: `The Sports Authority of Karnataka released ₹7.94 crore in grants exceeding the ₹25 lakh annual financial ceiling — including ₹1 crore to a film cricket association — without Cabinet sanction. SAK and GETHNAA failed to submit Utilisation Certificates for ₹94.40 crore of grants received over 2019–24. Records for ₹8.46 crore in cash awards were not produced for audit. Four District Stadium Management Committees held ₹30.79 crore in user-fee revenues idle in bank accounts while stadium maintenance went unperformed.`,
        actual: `₹7.94 Cr released beyond ₹25 lakh annual ceiling; ₹94.40 Cr grants without UCs (SAK + GETHNAA); ₹8.46 Cr award records withheld from audit; ₹30.79 Cr DSMC revenues lying idle; ₹4.54 Cr ineligible incentives paid.`,
        reportExcerpt: `"the expenditure of ₹7.94 crore released by the Chairman was beyond the annual financial ceiling of ₹25 lakh… SAK and GETHNAA had received grant-in-aid amounting to ₹83.57 crore and ₹15.85 crore respectively during 2019-20 to 2023-24… no UCs along with Audited expenditure statement were submitted… Four out of eight sampled DSMCs earned revenue by collection of user fees… lying unutilised in the bank accounts… No maintenance activity of the stadium was undertaken during this period."`,
