        parameter: `Housing completion, construction quality in tribal areas, and beneficiary grievance redressal`,
        finding: `Of 23.8 lakh rural housing units sanctioned under PMAY-G in Rajasthan, 36% remained incomplete after the 3-year completion deadline. In tribal districts of southern Rajasthan (Dungarpur, Banswara, Pratapgarh, Udaipur — the Bhil heartland), completion rates were only 48% with quality inspections revealing 32% of "completed" houses had structural issues: roof collapse risk, inadequate plinth height in flood-prone areas, and walls using sub-standard clay mixed with sand rather than brick. 28% of grievances registered on the AwaasSoft portal had received no response within 60 days. The failure is partly attributable to the 2023 election-year administrative discontinuity — the outgoing Congress government accelerated approvals in the final quarter before the December 2023 assembly elections, creating a bulge of approvals without construction capacity to match.`,
