                status: 'partial',
                note: 'ERCP — ₹37,247 crore, linking Parvati, Kali Sindh, Chambal and their tributaries to supply 13 south-east Rajasthan districts — was the Gehlot government\'s signature infrastructure project. Survey, DPR and initial tenders were done; GoJ deposited its 10% share. The project was stalled because BJP\'s MP government (CM Shivraj Singh Chouhan) refused to sign a water-sharing agreement, arguing upstream flows in the Kali Sindh belong to MP farmers. Gehlot publicly clashed with the Centre and MP over ERCP designation; Congress blamed BJP for politically blocking Rajasthan\'s water interests. As of mid-2026, under BJP\'s Bhajan Lal Sharma government, the same inter-state dispute persists despite both states now being BJP-governed. The renamed Parvati-Kali Sindh-Chambal Link (under Ken-Betwa framework) covers only 3 of ERCP\'s 13 target districts.',
                noteHi: 'ERCP: ₹37,247 करोड़। सर्वे, DPR, टेंडर हुए। MP की सहमति नहीं — कली सिंध जल बंटवारा विवाद। BJP और कांग्रेस दोनों के राज में अधूरी। 2026 में भी रुकी।',
