                status: 'partial',
                note: 'Rajasthan consistently ranks among India\'s top 3 states for crimes against women (NCRB 2023: 40,738 cases — behind UP and Maharashtra). The Gehlot government\'s Rajasthan Garima Niti (2020) — addressing dignity for women and marginalised groups — was a policy framework rather than a legislation. Child marriage: Rajasthan has India\'s highest child marriage prevalence at 27.4% (NFHS-5) — despite being a signatory to the National Plan to End Child Marriage. Honour killing cases (particularly in Jat-Gurjar belt of Bharatpur, Alwar, Sikar) remain consistently under-reported and under-prosecuted. Dalit women atrocity cases — particularly in Barmer, Nagaur and Jodhpur rural areas — increased 18% under the Congress term and were central to Opposition criticism. Mahila Samarth scheme provided training but structural violence indicators worsened. BJP has continued women-safety rhetoric without addressing the structural factors.',
