          note: `Bihar is India's 12th-largest state economy despite being the 3rd most populous state (13.1 crore). Per-capita GSDP of ~₹60,000 is the 2nd lowest in India after Manipur — less than one-third of the national average. The economy is driven by agriculture (~28% of GSDP), government services (~22%), and construction/remittances. Bihar has no significant industrial base — the post-1947 decision to keep industries in Jharkhand (which was carved out of Bihar in 2000) left the rump Bihar state economically hollowed out.`,
