                promiseHi: 'बिहार परिवहन कार्यालयों का आधुनिकीकरण; वाहन पंजीकरण और DL में भ्रष्टाचार समाप्त',
                status: 'partial',
                note: 'Bihar\'s District Transport Offices (DTOs) are among India\'s most cited sources of public-interface corruption — vehicle registration, fitness certificates, driving licences and permit issuance. CAG Transport Bihar (Report 5/2025) found: ₹1,240 crore in motor vehicle tax (MVT) and registration fee leakage over 5 years due to under-valuation of commercial vehicles; 38% of issued driving licences in 12 sampled DTOs could not be cross-verified with the national driving licence database (possibly fraudulent); fitness certificate racket — 62% of commercial vehicles receiving fitness certificates in Muzaffarpur, Patna and Bhagalpur DTOs were found non-roadworthy on surprise inspection. Digital reforms (SARATHI, VAHAN portals) have made some processes faceless but DTOs retain physical gatekeeping at multiple stages.',
