                note: 'Mission Bhagiratha — one of the largest rural drinking water projects in Indian history — was the BRS government\'s flagship infrastructure promise. Launched 2016, completed (99.6%) by 2019. The scheme piped water from the Krishna and Godavari rivers to every rural household and habitation in Telangana: 2.53 crore rural people across 26,055 villages. Scale: 1.42 crore new connections, 36,000 km pipeline, 7,500+ overhead tanks. Investment: ₹43,791 crore (GoT + NABARD loans). By 2021, Telangana achieved 80.6% household tap water connectivity (NFHS-5) — significantly above the national 43.5% average. Remaining challenge: distribution pressure (last-mile delivery) and water quality — CAG found fluoride contamination in 12% of Nalgonda/Suryapet district taps (2023). Mission Bhagiratha won a United Nations Public Service Award (2018).',
                noteHi: 'Mission Bhagiratha: ₹43,791 करोड़; 1.42 करोड़ कनेक्शन; 36,000 किमी पाइपलाइन। NFHS-5: 80.6% नल जल (राष्ट्रीय 43.5%)। UN Public Service Award 2018। CAG 2023: 12% टोंटियों में fluoride।',
