                note: 'Haryana contributes 20-25% of Delhi\'s winter air pollution through paddy stubble burning (Karnal, Kaithal, Ambala, Kurukshetra districts) — an annual October-November crisis that the BJP 2019 government promised to address. GoH disbursed ₹1,000/acre Happy Seeder incentive to 2.3 lakh farmers (2022-23) — above target — but overall stubble burning incidents fell only 14% in 2023 vs 2019 (Punjab + Haryana combined). The Aravalli forests — India\'s oldest mountain range, 650 km from Delhi to Gujarat — face a unique legal threat: 1992 Punjab Land Preservation Act exemptions (PLPA) allow construction in Aravalli in Haryana\'s Gurugram, Faridabad, and Nuh districts. The Supreme Court\'s Aravalli Protection Order (2019) ordered demolition of 10,000+ illegal structures — enforcement has been slow.',
                noteHi: 'हरियाणा: दिल्ली शीतकालीन AQI का 20-25% (पराली जलाना)। ₹1,000/एकड़ Happy Seeder: 2.3 लाख किसान। पराली घटनाएं: 14% कमी (लक्ष्य से बहुत कम)। SC अरावली आदेश (2019): 10,000+ अवैध संरचना ध्वंस — धीमा प्रवर्तन।',
