          note: `The Periyar river at Eloor-Edayar (Ernakulam district) is Kerala's most polluted industrial corridor — housing Hindustan Insecticides, Fertilisers and Chemicals Travancore (FACT), Hindustan Latex, BPCL, and 247 other industrial units. CPCB classified the stretch as one of India's 100 most polluted river segments. The Chaliyar river (Malappuram) was severely polluted for decades by the Grasim Industries rayon factory (Mavoor) — the factory closed in 2001 after sustained protests, and the Chaliyar has partially recovered. Kerala's rivers face dual threats: industrial pollution upstream and plastic/sewage pollution in urban stretches near Kochi and Kozhikode.`,
