          note: `Loktak Lake is Manipur's ecological heart — home to the Keibul Lamjao National Park (floating national park on phumdis — the only such in the world), where the endangered Brow-antlered deer (Sangai, Cervus eldii eldii — <260 individuals) lives on floating biomass islands. The lake receives untreated Imphal city sewage (180 MLD/day), agricultural runoff, and has 35% of its surface colonised by phumdis that block sunlight and oxygen. The Ithai Barrage (built 1983 for Loktak Hydroelectric Power) raised the lake's water level permanently — drowning traditional fishing communities and facilitating phumdi spread. A Ramsar Site since 1990, Loktak's ecological status continues to deteriorate despite international conservation concern.`,
