                status: 'partial',
                note: 'BJP 2017 came to power on an explicit anti-Ibobi (Okram Ibobi Singh — Congress CM for 15 years, 2002-17) governance narrative. IBI\'s government was associated with chronic blockades, rampant corruption in public works contracts, and the sclerotic Indo-Myanmar trade facilitation at Moreh. BJP\'s governance claims: (1) e-tendering for all contracts above ₹1 lakh (implemented 2018); (2) Direct Benefit Transfer for all welfare schemes (implemented 2019); (3) Cabinet review of 12,000 pending government cases (completed 2020). Anti-corruption: EOW (Economic Offences Wing) filed 48 new corruption cases (2017-22), including against former ministers. However CM N. Biren Singh\'s own government faced allegations: the 2021 MANISHA (Manipur Infrastructure Society) land irregularities case (₹340 crore worth of public land allegedly allocated irregularly to private parties — CAG Manipur 2022 flagged this). The 2023 ethnic conflict — which many observers attribute partly to governance failures (Biren government\'s handling of Meitei ST demand) — is the most serious governance failure of the 2017-22 BJP term.',
