                status: 'partial',
                note: 'Meghalaya\'s MGNREGS faces a unique structural challenge: under the Sixth Schedule, traditional Khasi-Jaintia village councils (dorbar shnong — presided over by the Syiem, the traditional chief) have formal legal authority over community land and resource decisions in scheduled tribal areas. MGNREGS work selection — requiring village-level asset creation — is routed through the dorbar shnong, which CAG 2025 found had, in 38% of sampled panchayats, approved work plans primarily benefiting the Syiem\'s own family and allies. The NPP government\'s reforms: (1) introduced a parallel online work-demand registration system bypassing dorbar shnong approval for individual job cards; (2) piloted a Women\'s MGNREGS Committee (Waheh Sor) in 120 Khasi Hills villages to reduce elite capture. These reforms helped — but the dorbar shnong\'s constitutional status under the Sixth Schedule makes fundamental reform politically and legally impossible without community consent.',
                noteHi: 'dorbar shnong: 38% panchayat में CAG ने elite capture पाया। NPP ने online job card + Waheh Sor महिला समिति (120 गांव)। Sixth Schedule संवैधानिक दर्जे से मौलिक सुधार असंभव।',
