                note: 'The NPP 2018 government inherited a severely under-resourced health system. The Meghalaya Health Assurance Scheme (MHAS) was launched 2018: ₹3 lakh/family cover for BPL households at empanelled hospitals — 1.8 lakh families enrolled by 2023. CHC functional 24x7: only 22 of 52 CHCs achieved round-the-clock delivery (by CAG definition: doctor + nurse + lab + pharmacy all simultaneously available). Under-resourced CHCs in South Garo Hills and North Garo Hills struggle with vacancy and transport. The state\'s biggest health achievement: Mawkyrwat Civil Hospital (South West Khasi Hills, Meghalaya\'s remotest district headquarters) received a new 50-bed block, O&G and paediatric wards — operational 2021, reducing maternal deaths in the district from 34 (2018) to 12 (2023). Specialist shortage: 54% vacancy at district hospitals.',
