                note: 'Meghalaya is a Special Category State (SCS) — one of 11 states receiving enhanced Central assistance: 90% grant, 10% loan ratio (vs 60:40 for other states). The 14th Finance Commission (2015) discontinued the formal SCS category but maintained the enhanced NE devolution; the 15th Finance Commission retained this. NEC (North East Council) allocated ₹680 crore to Meghalaya for 2018-23 — infrastructure (NH-6, Shillong bypass), connectivity (power line Palatana-Shillong) and tourism. Conrad Sangma, as NPP chief with national coalition importance (NPP is part of NDA), leveraged Delhi relationships for NEC approvals. Key success: North East Special Infrastructure Development Scheme (NESIDS) funding for Shillong bypass (₹1,890 crore — approval obtained 2021). SCS financial model: 78% of Meghalaya\'s revenue is Central-transferred — making the state fiscally dependent but insulated from own-revenue shocks.',
