                status: 'partial',
                note: 'The Naga political conflict — India\'s oldest insurgency, dating to 1956 when the Naga National Council (NNC) under A.Z. Phizo declared independence — has shaped Nagaland\'s entire political economy. The NDPP was formed in 2017 specifically as the political vehicle to deliver the Naga solution under PM Modi, replacing the Neiphiu Rio-led NPF. The 2015 Framework Agreement between GoI and NSCN(IM) — signed by PM Modi and NSCN(IM) General Secretary Th. Muivah — was the most significant peace breakthrough in the 60-year conflict. The 2018-23 NDPP government\'s promise was to translate the Framework Agreement into a final accord. This did not happen: (1) NSCN(IM) insists on a separate Naga flag and constitution — GoI refuses both; (2) the NNPG (Working Committee of 7 smaller Naga groups) signed a partial agreement in 2020 (without flag/constitution demands) but NSCN(IM) rejected this as insufficient. The 2021 breakdown: GoI interlocutor R.N. Ravi was replaced after he publicly accused NSCN(IM) of bad faith. Nagaland civil society (Naga Mothers\' Association, Naga Students\' Federation) have demanded a timeline — none has been set. The ceasefire with NSCN(IM) (since 1997) continues without violation. The Naga solution remains the central unresolved promise of every Nagaland government since 1997.',
