        finding: `Tamil Nadu's CMCHIS — which covers 1.7 crore families (below-poverty-line and near-poverty threshold) at a state cost of ~₹820 crore per year — was found to have systematic claim fraud by empanelled private hospitals. Of 272 empanelled hospitals sampled, 67 (25%) had billed for procedures with no corresponding patient discharge records — 18,200 ghost surgeries in the audit period. Total suspected fraudulent or inflated claims amounted to ₹820 crore over 2019-23. Average billing was 38% above procedure-wise package rates. Beneficiary eligibility databases were not verified against family income updates — 32,000 ineligible above-threshold families were covered.`,
