            value: `70% of India's jute production; largest rice bowl in India`,
            note: `West Bengal produces 70% of India's jute (Nadia, Murshidabad, North 24 Parganas), 15% of its rice, 30% of its potatoes and 90% of its Darjeeling tea (Darjeeling, Jalpaiguri GI-tagged). Agriculture is a more stable pillar of WB's economy than in most industrialised states — the rice-jute-potato trinity provides livelihoods to ~2 crore farming households. However, jute mills (operating near Kolkata) have declined from 200 in the 1960s to ~70 today — creating structural unemployment in jute-mill towns.`,
            noteHi: `West Bengal भारत के जूट का 70% उत्पादन करता है (Nadia, Murshidabad, North 24 Parganas), 15% चावल, 30% आलू और 90% Darjeeling चाय (Darjeeling, Jalpaiguri GI-tagged)। कृषि WB की अर्थव्यवस्था का एक अधिक स्थिर स्तंभ है — चावल-जूट-आलू त्रिमूर्ति ~2 करोड़ कृषि परिवारों को आजीविका देती है। हालाँकि, जूट मिलें 1960 के दशक में 200 से घटकर आज ~70 हो गई हैं।`,
            source: `West Bengal Agriculture Dept. Annual Report 2024; Tea Board of India; CMIE`,
